From 9676ca645911d569f0f022728b572950983187ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:26:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: operator_message + ops_export for ops-notify relay
 (Phase 7b, v0.18.0) (#25)

The repair bot's notifications are silently dropped on both hosts: strategy
envs keep ALERTS_ENABLED=false by policy, so its publish() calls reach zero
channels. Phase 7b routes them through ops-notify instead -- the strategy
writes a snapshot, ops-notify (which owns the maintenance channel) relays it.
This is the shared half.

- The fleet error catalog becomes package data (catalog/ ->
  src/trade_alerts/catalog/, pyproject package-data). Strategy hosts install
  trade-alerts non-editable from a git tag, so the repo-level file never
  reached them. load_error_catalog() with no path reads the packaged copy.
- Catalog entries gain an optional operator_message {what, direction,
  steps[]}: plain-language text for the phone. Written for momentum's three
  repair-bot conditions (R1/R2/R4). New invariants: all three parts
  non-empty, never on R0, the momentum three must have one.
- New trade_alerts.ops_export: build_ops_export() turns a strategy's fleet
  event log + request queue into fleet-ops-export/v1 (R1-R4 notices of the
  last 7 days with a fully rendered text, keyed by event_id; open requests
  with the plain-language parts); write_ops_export() replaces it atomically
  at 0644. Schema in schemas/fleet-ops-export-v1.schema.json.

229 tests (206 -> +23).

Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
